WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.360
Let’s talk about Donald Trump

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.720
and what he might do now that he’s lost the election.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.440
The big American news networks

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.640
did the math and 
called Biden’s win. 

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.440
But Trump is contesting 
some results in court. 

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.280
So can Trump still 
win in court?

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.560
What can he do with 
the time  

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.320
he has left in the 
White House? 

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.520
And what if he 
refuses to leave?

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.160
No presidential candidate 

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.760
in the history of 
the United States

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.160
has ever outright 
refused to concede.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.880
Richard Nixon bowed out 
even after accusing 

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.800
John F Kennedy and the Democrats of rigging votes.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.320
Vice President Al Gore accepted the Supreme Court’s

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.640
ruling that George W Bush won in Florida.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.160
That was after a 
long legal battle

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.720
and a recount that
 came up with

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.400
a razor-thin difference 
of 537 votes.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.800
But Trump’s not giving up. 

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.840
And there are things 
he can still do.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.960
In a tight race, a candidate can request a recount. 

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.000
Georgia has already 
agreed to one.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.920
But recounts have only 
ever led to totals

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.920
that change by a 
few dozen votes 

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.400
sometimes hundreds.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.080
Biden’s lead in 
battleground states 

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.080
is in the tens of thousands.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.040
A candidate can also 
file a lawsuit  

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.760
if they suspect irregularities.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.240
The Trump campaign has challenged electoral processes

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.440
in several states over things like Republican observers

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.960
not getting close enough to the counting process

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.640
ballots - that 
are otherwise valid -  

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.560
being counted after Election Day, and allegations of fraud. 

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.560
but lawsuits in Michigan, Georgia, Wisconsin  

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.040
and Arizona have
 already failed.  

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.760
Still - Trump’s lawyer 
Rudy Giuliani says 

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.760
they’re going to
keep going.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.160
The election timetable
 means legal battles 

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.600
can’t go on forever.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.080
In most states recounts and court challenges 

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.240
have to wrap up by 
December 8.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.600
Dec 14 is when electors from each state come together

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.320
as the Electoral College 
to cast their votes.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.240
The presidential race has been called for Biden 

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.120
because enough
 Democrat electors

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.760
are expected to 
confirm his victory.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.000
After all that Trump can make all the noise he wants 

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.200
but it won’t affect who takes the Office of the President.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.920
He doesn’t even have to concede publicly. 

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.440
That’s just a - usually - respected tradition.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.640
Whatever happens, it’ll all be over - officially -     

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.360
when Trump’s term ends at noon on January 20, 2021.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.560
That’s when the new president is sworn in.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.960
So what happens if Trump refuses to leave?

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.960
But Trump still has 10 
weeks left in office.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.400
And a lot can happen 
in 10 weeks.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.880
He’ll still be commander-in-chief

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.600
and can make important foreign policy decisions.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.000
George Bush Sr 
for example

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.640
sent troops to Somalia 
in his final weeks

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.520
and Jimmy Carter ended the Iran hostage crisis.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.880
Trump can also declassify information

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.240
and use the power of the presidential pardon 

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.600
to free people from 
prison or stop a trial

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.320
if it’s a federal case.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.320
The president had to know he was in trouble

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.560
when even Fox News
his favourite TV channel

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.000
called his defeat.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.120
Some of Trump’s allies 

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.640
including the Israeli prime minister 

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.880
have already 
congratulated Biden.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.680
None of that means Trump can’t put up a fight.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:58.840
It’s his right.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.640
But it’s probably not going to get him very far.

